vidence: node1 baseline, ack, changed identity, recovered state","status":"satisfied","summary":"Pre-restart kern.boottime (17:53:52) and healthy pf rule/log state captured; configctl system reboot dispatched and acknowledged; SSH timed out during the transition then reconnected with a new kern.boottime (18:00:30), proving an actual reboot; post-restart pf block/pass rules and interfaces were intact, and a fresh node2-originated tcp/23 block was logged and persisted, directly demonstrating recovered routing, policy, and logging state. Cross-checked against the fixed after-executor boot-identity snapshot, which matches.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f5cb57bc07ae40b8","cmd-513b87740e79422e","cmd-1fe125dbb73e4b6e","cmd-9f46e0aec35f425f","cmd-8353cea849bd41e6","cmd-a5ecad17625b4629","cmd-20d06d92fc364c1a","cmd-7b1da708d4544ab3"]},{"id":"restart-node2","requirement":"Provider-wide restart evidence: node2 baseline, ack, changed identity, recovered state","status":"satisfied","summary":"Pre-restart boot_id (92ec88af...) captured; reboot dispatched via backgrounded 'reboot' command with an explicit acknowledgement printed before the connection would drop; post-restart boot_id (95b30093...) differs, proving a real reboot; connectivity to node1's lan-a gateway was re-verified by ping after reapplying the (expectedly ephemeral) IP. Matches the fixed after-executor snapshot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d1f948764e844410","cmd-5400aeace8c84424","cmd-d9067fb49eac47be"]},{"id":"restart-node3","requirement":"Provider-wide restart evidence: node3 baseline, ack, changed identity, recovered state","status":"satisfied","summary":"Pre-restart boot_id (242af11e...) captured; reboot dispatched and acknowledged; post-restart boot_id (3b2dd459...) differs, proving a real reboot; connectivity to node1's lan-b gateway re-verified, and a final full end-to-end check (node2->node3 ping plus renewed tcp/23 block) confirmed the whole topology and policy survived all three restarts. Matches the fixed after-executor snapshot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-96072b6ba0e54f6d","cmd-748a9086b3544b8a","cmd-8d42fe3a10d44a95","cmd-3d6f5a4291e44f73"]}],"confidence":0.85,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.82,"summary":"Most state-changing commands map clearly to a task purpose: ephemeral ifconfig IP assignment on node1 (cmd-46328863e80a469a) preceded and was superseded by the persistent config.xml edits (cmd-67e85fc519fd48e9, cmd-685e521e2a114ae0); node2/node3 ip addr/ip route additions were necessary, low-risk test-client configuration expected to be non-persistent on these simple Ubuntu hosts and were correctly redone after their own reboots (cmd-d9067fb49eac47be, cmd-8d42fe3a10d44a95). One ineffective mutation attempt occurred (cmd-513b87740e79422e's 'configctl reboot &' returned 'Action not allowed or missing' and had no effect, immediately corrected by cmd-1fe125dbb73e4b6e using the working 'configctl system reboot' invocation) — bounded and harmless. A background tcpdump diagnostic (cmd-c097e79df73b463a) hit a 120s proxy timeout; it was a bounded packet-count-limited capture (self-terminating) and a working replacement was started and properly killed afterward (cmd-5804c60253d148f5, cmd-b190bbc9f6954dbd), so any orphaned process was low-risk and self-limiting. An initial log-extraction destination (/var/log/telnet_block.log, cmd-828d783d027b4277) was found to be lost after reboot because /var/log is tmpfs; this was a reasonable exploration promptly corrected by moving to the persistent /root/telnet_block.log (cmd-7b1da708d4544ab3), and no broken or conflicting state remained. Small helper scripts (/tmp/add_ifaces.py, add_rules.py, add_block23.py) and tcpdump/reboot log files were left in /tmp on node1; these are typical bounded automation artifacts, not shown as growing residue in the fixed temporary-files snapshot diff (which only shows expected tmpcfd_* churn), and pose no functional or security risk.","evidence_ids":["cmd-46328863e80a469a","cmd-67e85fc519fd48e9","cmd-685e521e2a114ae0","cmd-513b87740e79422e","cmd-1fe125dbb73e4b6e","cmd-c097e79df73b463a","cmd-5804c60253d148f5","cmd-b190bbc9f6954dbd","cmd-828d783d027b4277","cmd-7b1da708d4544ab3","cmd-d9067fb49eac47be","cmd-8d42fe3a10d44a95"]},"overall_summary":"All four material task outcomes are directly and coherently satisfied: node1 routes lan-a<->lan-b traffic (proven with live ping/tcpdump), tcp/23 is refused in both directions while other traffic (ssh) still passes, every refused attempt is captured by pf's native logged block rule and persisted to /root/telnet_block.log on node1, and a specific log entry attributable to a node2-originated attempt (source 10.60.1.2) was shown. The independent provider-wide restart protocol was also fully and correctly executed and evidenced for all three nodes, each showing a pre-restart baseline, an acknowledgement, a changed boot identity, and directly observed recovered routing/policy/logging state, consistent with the fixed after-prepare/after-executor boot-identity snapshots. Operational hygiene is good: a few exploratory or ineffective commands occurred (an invalid reboot action, a tcpdump proxy timeout, a tmpfs log-path mistake) but each was bounded, low-risk, and promptly corrected without leaving damaging or conflicting residue.","limitations":["The /root/telnet_block.log persistence mechanism is a manually-triggered extraction script rather than a continuously running logging daemon; the underlying pf filter log (with the 'log' rule keyword) does capture every block automatically, but /root/telnet_block.log itself only reflects entries extracted at the moments the executor ran the extraction command, so attempts made without a follow-up extraction would not appear in that specific file until re-run.","Minor /tmp artifacts (helper python scripts, tcpdump/reboot logs) created on node1 during the session were not explicitly confirmed removed, though the fixed temporary-files snapshot diff does not show them accumulating as persistent residue."]},"ttft_ms":54650,"type":"result","duration_ms":121049,"uuid":"50150f1d-f514-46b9-984f-e20fe6580c36","ttft_stream_ms":2625,"time_to_request_ms":45,"first_content_frame_ms":3413,"queued_turn_count":0}
